## 3. Content Blocks — Text

### Add a text block
- Click **"+ Text"** in the editor toolbar.

### Edit content
- Click the preview area to switch to edit mode.
- Click outside or press Tab to return to preview.
- Markdown is rendered as HTML in preview (fenced code, tables, line breaks supported).

### Formatting toolbar
| Button | Shortcut | Action |
|--------|----------|--------|
| **B** | `Ctrl+B` | Wraps selected text in `**` (bold) |
| **I** | `Ctrl+I` | Wraps selected text in `*` (italic) |
| **H1** | — | Inserts `# ` at cursor |
| **H2** | — | Inserts `## ` at cursor |
| **<>** | — | Wraps selection in `` ` `` (inline code) |
| **🔗** | — | Creates `[text](url)` Markdown link |
| **•** | — | Inserts `- ` (bullet list item) |

- Formatting applies to the **currently focused text block** only.

### Delete a block
- Click the **"×"** button in the block header (no confirmation, undoable).

### Resize a block
- **Bottom resize handle** — drag up/down to change height, drag left/right to change width.
- **Bottom-right corner** (24px dotted area) — 2D resize: drag to change both width and height simultaneously.
- **Right edge** — hover near the right edge of any block (cursor changes to ↔), then click and drag to change width.

### Canvas behavior
- The canvas is **vertically infinite** — scrolling near the bottom extends it automatically (no horizontal scrollbar).
- **Right edge is a hard boundary** — blocks cannot be dragged or resized past the right edge of the canvas.
- Position (`pos_x`, `pos_y`) is persisted in the database.

### Move blocks (free-form canvas)
- Blocks are positioned on a **free-form canvas** (no layout constraints).
- Drag the **"⋮⋮"** handle to freely reposition a block.
- Blocks can overlap and be placed anywhere within the canvas bounds.
- **Clicking** a block brings it to the front (z-order).

---

## 4. Content Blocks — Tables

### Add a table block
- Click **"+ Table"** in the toolbar.

### Modify table structure
- **"+ Row"** / **"- Row"** — add/remove the last row (minimum 1 row).
- **"+ Col"** / **"- Col"** — add/remove the last column (minimum 1 column).

### Edit cells
- Click any cell and type. Cells support plain text (not rendered Markdown).

### Persistence
- Table content is auto-saved and restored on page reload.

---

## 5. Content Blocks — Lists & Checkboxes (Tasks)

### Add a list/checkbox block
- Click **"+ List"** in the toolbar.

### Task operations
- **Check/uncheck** a task via its checkbox.
- **Edit task text** directly in a **multi-line text area** (auto-grows as you type).
- **Set recurrence** via the dropdown: `none`, `daily`, `weekly`, `monthly`.
- **Delete** a task with **"X"** button (no confirmation, undoable).
- **Add** a new task with **"+ Add Task"** button in the block header (alongside the alignment & delete-block buttons).

### Task row interactions
- **Auto-grow** — the text area expands vertically when content exceeds the current row height (fires on every keystroke); never shrinks automatically.
- **Column resize** — drag the thin vertical `⋮` handle between the text area and the sidebar to change text width (minimum 100 px, capped at container width).
- **Row resize** — drag the thin horizontal handle at the bottom of any task row to set a fixed height (overrides auto-grow; row will not auto-grow taller while fixed).
- **Sidebar layout** — each task row has a sidebar (Recur label+dropdown + Delete "X") fixed at the right edge; all sidebars are **vertically aligned** across every row of the same list block.

### Recurring tasks
- When a recurring task is checked, a **copy** is created with the due date shifted forward (daily=+1d, weekly=+7d, monthly=+30d).
- Verify: check a weekly task → a new unchecked task appears with the same text.

### Undo for tasks
- Deleting a task can be undone via **Edit → Undo Delete** (`Ctrl+Shift+Z`), same as page/block deletion.
- Each undo restores the most recently deleted item (task, block, or page).

---

## 6. Template System

### Save a page as template
- **Page → Save Page as Template** → enter a name.
- All content blocks (text, tables, tasks) are captured as JSON.

### Insert a template into current page
- Click **"Template"** button in the editor toolbar → select a template.
- The template's blocks are appended to the current page.

### Bulk insert template into multiple pages
- **Ctrl+click** / **Shift+click** to select multiple pages in the sidebar.
- Right-click → **"Insert Template into Selected (N)"** → pick one template.
- The template is applied to **every selected page**.

### Persistence
- Templates survive app restart (stored in SQLite `templates` table).

---

## 7. Auto-Save

- Content is auto-saved every **N ms** (default: 1000ms, configurable in Settings).
- Any content change in text blocks/table cells triggers the save timer.
- Navigate away from a page and back → content should be preserved.

---

## 8. Settings

- **File → Settings...** opens a dialog with:
  - **Week start day** (used by bulk "Weeks" creation).
  - **Auto-save interval** (500–10000 ms, step 500).
  - **Font size** (10–32; requires restart).
- Settings persist in `settings.json`.

---

## 9. Window Layout & Responsiveness

- The splitter between sidebar and editor is **draggable**.
- Window resizes gracefully; test at **1024×768** and **1920×1080**.
- Sidebar has `minWidth=200` and `maxWidth=400`.

